  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Freeze and free – with a ball",
  "description": "Everyone has a ball and moves freely inside a box. A hunter (red) also has a ball and tries to hit the others' balls by passing at them. If your ball is hit you freeze and stand still with your foot on the ball. A teammate frees you by dribbling over and touching you.\n\nThe youngest can roll the ball with their hands instead of dribbling. Change the hunter often, and use two hunters with a big group. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Look up – where is the hunter and where is there free space?"
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Keep the ball close so you can turn quickly."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Help your teammates – whoever frees the most wins."
    }
  ],
